18	/**
19	 * One customer's whole estate, normalised into a single list.
20	 *
21	 * The four products live in genuinely different tables — a VPS and a game
22	 * server are both `Server` rows told apart by `gamePlanId`, shared hosting is
23	 * a `HostingAccount`, and the free Minecraft tier is its own
24	 * `FreeMinecraftServer` — so this is the one place that flattens them into a
25	 * shape a single list can render. Everything below is read from the record;
26	 * nothing is inferred where the data doesn't exist (hosting has no region
27	 * column, so its location is geo-resolved from the node's real public IP the
28	 * same way the primary node's location was confirmed, and is left blank when
29	 * that lookup can't answer).
